# RSA Algorithm

This experiment demonstrates the implementation of the RSA (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman) algorithm using HTML and JavaScript.

# Implementation
  Language: HTML, JavaScript
  Algorithm: RSA
  Type: Asymmetric Encryption
  Input: Two prime numbers and a message
  Output: Public key, exponent, private key, and cipher text

 # Working

The program takes two prime numbers p and q and calculates:

n = p × q
φ(n) = (p − 1) × (q − 1)
Selects a public exponent e
Calculates the private key d

# The message is then encrypted using:

C = M^e mod n

where M is the message and C is the cipher text.

# Example
p = 53
q = 59
Message = 89

Public Key = 3127
Exponent = 3
Private Key = 2011
Cipher Text = 1394
